      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TOUR DE MOON (3) was well supported first-up at Murray Bridge when sent out fav but ultimately left himself with too much to do in the straight, closing off well into second. Is a second-up winner and if Callow can have him a pair or two closer this time he will prove awfully hard to stop. OIE DE TOULOUSE (2) was an eye-catcher first-up in town in what has proven a very strong maiden. Less effective second-up but was much better third-up when closing off strongly from the back into a midfield finish. Has been kept fresh with 35 days in-between. Watch for her bursting through late. SCOOTATHEWOOTA (1) was a good winner second-up when only seeing clear air late, then got too far back last time but was strong at the end. Pannell reuniting is a positive and the inside draw helps. GIN RUMMY (5) failed to live up to expectation first-up in testing conditions but is better than that and is drawn much kinder. Worth another look. ROADKING (4) returns and looks best of the rest.",
